 🚁 Drone Finder - Pocket Edition

An EdgeTX Lua script that turns your radio into a lost-drone locator using ELRS/CRSF RSSI telemetry — adapted for the RadioMaster Pocket (128×64 monochrome LCD, button/scroll-wheel navigation).

> This is a derivative of [Drone Finder](https://github.com/p3gass/Drone-Finder-ELRS) by michalek.me, originally built for the RadioMaster TX15's color touchscreen. See [Credits & License](#credits--license) below.

---

 ✨ Features

- 📡 Works with ELRS/CRSF telemetry (`1RSS`, `RSNR`, or `RQly`, whichever your RX exposes)
- 📶 Horizontal signal-strength bar gauge with percent readout
- 🔔 Geiger-style audio feedback — beep rate increases as signal gets stronger
- 🎛 Scroll-wheel click (ENTER) toggles sound on/off
- 🔋 Battery voltage display with automatic cell-count detection
- ⚠️ Low-voltage warning (blinking/inverted text below 3.4V/cell)
- 🖥 Compact layout built for 128×64 monochrome displays — no touchscreen required

 Why this fork exists

The original script uses EdgeTX's `lvgl` API for its UI — circular gauges, RGB color fills, touch-driven toggles. That API only exists on color touchscreen EdgeTX radios (TX15, TX16S, Zorro, etc.). The RadioMaster Pocket has a 1.6" 128×64 monochrome LCD with no touch panel, so `lvgl` is unavailable and the original UI never renders.

This version replaces the entire UI layer with the standard `lcd.draw*` API that every EdgeTX mono radio supports, and reworks the layout to fit 128×64. Sensor detection, signal smoothing, and battery/cell logic are unchanged from the original.

 Installation

1. Copy `Drone-Finder-Pocket.lua` to `/SCRIPTS/TELEMETRY/` on your radio's SD card.
2. On the radio: open your model, go to the Telemetry screens, add a new screen, set its type to Script, and select this file.
3. Make sure ELRS telemetry is actually reaching the radio:
   - RX bound and linked (solid LED, not blinking)
   - ExpressLRS Telemetry Ratio set to `Std` (or tighter, e.g. `1:16`) — not `Off`
   - Run Discover New Sensors under Model Setup → Telemetry after changing the ratio

 Usage

- The bar gauge shows signal strength as a percentage; the number above the bar is the same value.
- Sound gets faster/higher-pitched as signal strengthens — walk toward the beeping.
- Press **ENT** (scroll wheel click) on the telemetry screen to mute/unmute the beeper.
- Low cell voltage (<3.40V/cell) blinks the battery line so you don't miss it mid-search.

 Requirements

- RadioMaster Pocket (or any EdgeTX radio with a 128×64 monochrome LCD)
- EdgeTX firmware with Lua telemetry script support
- ELRS receiver reporting `1RSS`, `RSNR`, or `RQly` via CRSF telemetry

